    "answer": {
      "short": "The cylinder, by $0.57\\,\\mathrm{m}^3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}V_{\\text{cube}} &= Ah\\\\V_{\\text{cube}} &= (1\\times1)\\times1\\\\V_{\\text{cube}} &= 1\\,\\mathrm{m}^3\\\\V_{\\text{cylinder}} &= \\pi r^2h\\\\V_{\\text{cylinder}} &= \\pi\\times1^2\\times0.5\\\\V_{\\text{cylinder}} &= \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\,\\mathrm{m}^3\\end{align*}$$\nThe cylinder has the bigger volume.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Difference} &= \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-1\\right)\\mathrm{m}^3\\\\\\text{Difference} &\\approx0.57\\,\\mathrm{m}^3\\end{align*}$$",
